cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, its results or its figures, please cite this record and the related companion preprint. Do not reuse the companion DOI for this work."
title: "OTAZ III: The Gibbs Ledger - Exact Aggregation, a Sharp Impossibility Theorem, and Certified Error Budgets for Scored-Record Fusion"
abstract: >-
  A standalone mathematical study of one operator: a temperature-scaled softmax
  over scores normalising a weighted mean of values, carried alongside the scaled
  log-partition sum. The paper proves that the pair is a commutative monoid and
  merges exactly in any tree, that it is neither idempotent (a duplicate record
  adds beta^-1 ln 2) nor homogeneous (the defect is 2.1932 at lambda = 2), and
  then proves the negative result the title names: with value-only summaries the
  set of global values compatible with the reports is the convex hull of the
  reported values, the minimax merge rule is the midpoint, its worst-case error
  is half the range and is attained, and no rule does better. A ledger quantised
  to relative precision delta merges to within D delta / (1 - delta) for any
  number of shards. On the positive side the paper gives a temperature calculus
  (dV/dbeta = Cov(v,w), d2 lnZ / dbeta2 = Var(w)), a coarse-graining identity
  gap = beta^-1 H(pi) with its Shannon chain rule, an error non-amplification
  bound for the logit parametrisation, a composition of sampling and truncation
  into one certified interval, and the boundary of the quantum reading (dephasing
  contractivity, a Helstrom floor, no converse). Sixteen seeded experiments,
  52 unit tests and a 56-check independent verifier regenerate every reported
  number. Negative results are in the main text. No priority, peer-review or
  quantum-advantage claim is made.
